## Exercise 1 — `with`, deconstruction, and what stayed put

Edit `src/Lessons/V3CA01_Records/Ex1.cs`.

```csharp
public record Seat(string Row, int Number)
{
    public Seat NextSeat();
    public string Label();
    public bool SameRowAs(Seat other);
}
```

- `new Seat("A", 12).NextSeat()` -> `Seat { Row = A, Number = 13 }`
- `new Seat("A", 12).Label()` -> `"A12"`, written using the generated
  `Deconstruct` rather than the properties
- `new Seat("A", 12).SameRowAs(new Seat("A", 40))` -> `true`;
  `.SameRowAs(new Seat("B", 12))` -> `false`

The gate keeps a reference to the original seat, calls `NextSeat()` twice, and
then asserts the original still reads `A12` — plus that
`seat.NextSeat().NextSeat().Label()` is `"A14"`.

```
uv run dojo test csharp v3ca01_records_value_equality ex1
```

