## Exercise 7 — a record struct as a dictionary key

Edit `src/Lessons/V3CA01_Records/Ex7.cs`.

```csharp
public readonly record struct SkuKey(string Code)
{
    public bool Equals(SkuKey other);
    public override int GetHashCode();
}

public sealed class SkuIndex
{
    public void Add(string code, int stock);
    public bool TryLookup(string code, out int stock);
}
```

`SkuKey` compares and hashes **ordinal case-insensitively**, so `"AB-1"`,
`"ab-1"` and `"Ab-1"` are one key:

- `new SkuKey("AB-1") == new SkuKey("ab-1")` -> `true`
- `new SkuKey("AB-1").GetHashCode() == new SkuKey("ab-1").GetHashCode()` -> `true`
- `new SkuKey("AB-1") == new SkuKey("AB-2")` -> `false`

`SkuIndex` holds a `Dictionary<SkuKey, int>`. After
`Add("AB-1", 4)`, `TryLookup("ab-1", out int stock)` is `true` with `stock == 4`,
and `TryLookup("zz-9", out _)` is `false` with `stock == 0`.

Ordinal, not culture-sensitive: the gate runs one assertion under the Turkish
culture and expects `"I"` and `"i"` to stay two different keys.

```
uv run dojo test csharp v3ca01_records_value_equality ex7
```

