## Exercise 8 — `required`, `init` and a proven-non-null merge

Edit `src/Lessons/V3CA04_NullableReferences/Ex8.cs`.

```csharp
public sealed record DraftProfile(string? DisplayName, string? Email, string? Timezone);

public sealed class Profile
{
    public required string DisplayName { get; init; }
    public required string Email { get; init; }
    public required string Timezone { get; init; }

    public Profile() { }

    [SetsRequiredMembers]
    public Profile(string displayName, string email, string timezone);
}

public static class Profiles
{
    public static bool TryMerge(DraftProfile primary, DraftProfile fallback, out Profile? merged);
}
```

`TryMerge` takes the first non-null value for each member, preferring
`primary`. If any member is still null after both drafts, it returns `false`
and `merged` is `null`.

- primary `("ada", null, null)`, fallback `(null, "a@x", "UTC")` ->
  `true`, `Profile { DisplayName = ada, Email = a@x, Timezone = UTC }`
- primary `("ada", null, null)`, fallback `(null, "a@x", null)` -> `false`
- primary `("ada", "a@x", "UTC")`, fallback all null -> `true`

Rules: no `!` anywhere, no `ArgumentNullException` for the merged fields, and
the compiler must *prove* every member of the constructed `Profile` is
non-null. The gate also constructs a `Profile` with an object initialiser
missing `Timezone` in a separate file and asserts it fails to compile.

Then add a comment on what `[SetsRequiredMembers]` costs you: name the specific
thing that stops being checked.

